# --- build artifacts ---
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe

# --- secrets & local config ---
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
# NTAG AES keys must NEVER be committed. See CLAUDE.md "Kirmizi Cizgiler".
secrets/
*.aes
# The FILLED copy of deploy/examples/secret.example.yaml. That file carries the
# session key, the invite key and TAPPA_TAG_KEK -- the key that unwraps every
# plaque's NTAG AES key in the park, and the one value in this product whose loss is
# unrecoverable (deploy/examples/secret.example.yaml, ESCROW).
#
# 🔴 THE RULE IS "ANY secret-ish yaml UNDER deploy/, EXCEPT the .example ones", AND
# THE NARROW FORM WAS MEASURED TO BE INSUFFICIENT (2026-08-15, audit round 4). It
# used to list two exact paths, /deploy/secret.yaml and /deploy/k8s/secret.yaml. The
# template then MOVED to deploy/examples/, where the natural thing to type is
# `cp secret.example.yaml secret.yaml` -- and `git check-ignore -v
# deploy/examples/secret.yaml` came back COMMITTABLE. The guarantee this block
# claimed was true only for the directory the file no longer lived in.
#
# The pattern below is deliberately WIDER than any single filename, because the
# second mechanical net does not exist either: scripts/redline-check.sh does not scan
# deploy/ at all (that gap is a recorded open finding). This is the only automatic
# protection a filled copy has.
/deploy/**/*secret*.yaml
/deploy/*secret*.yaml
# ...but the value-free templates ARE committed, and must stay committed.
!/deploy/**/*.example.yaml
!/deploy/*.example.yaml

# --- generated CSS (built by make css) ---
/web/static/css/app.css

# --- go ---
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# --- local tooling downloaded by `make tools` ---
/.tools/

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# --- claude local overrides ---
.claude/settings.local.json
